Differential-algebraic models, initialization and events (@pe-dae-models: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @electrical-power-engineering, #source "../sources/Hybrid-Symbolic-Numeric-Power-Models-Cui.lingua#r_7XTYA62FQ8W2X448XXVFNPA7AK", #source "../sources/ANDES-Modeling-and-Analysis-Manual.lingua#r_5JM9DVGXWSD8645484SZP5XRSZ", #source "../sources/DPsim-Transient-and-Dynamic-Phasor-Methods.lingua#r_6Y8PGZBGJHGV3JHZ1Q8XC77RR3", #electrical-power-engineering "../conversion/Grid-following-current-control-synchronization-and-limits.lingua#r_6RBJ2AJVKVGPF9HP5XP3EHYY5T") { r_4EW7VDSRDD2E5S2VR886XWW2PZ
**Read:** [Hybrid Symbolic-Numeric Framework — Cui, Li and Tomsovic](../sources/Hybrid-Symbolic-Numeric-Power-Models-Cui.lingua#r_7XTYA62FQ8W2X448XXVFNPA7AK), entire paper and full case methods; [ANDES — dynamic modelling and analysis manual](../sources/ANDES-Modeling-and-Analysis-Manual.lingua#r_5JM9DVGXWSD8645484SZP5XRSZ), complete modelling, initialization, events and solver documentation; [DPsim — electromagnetic-transient and dynamic-phasor methods](../sources/DPsim-Transient-and-Dynamic-Phasor-Methods.lingua#r_6Y8PGZBGJHGV3JHZ1Q8XC77RR3), whole relevant model/domain and initialization methods.

Power dynamics often combine differential equipment/control states with algebraic network constraints. Write x_dot = f(x,y,u) and 0 = g(x,y,u), identify the physical meaning of each variable and check consistent initialization against a solved operating state. An algebraic solver residual and a dynamic integration error are different quantities.

Events change topology, control mode or limits and may require reinitializing algebraic variables while preserving the appropriate physical states. A switching instant can create a discontinuity or a model singularity; simply reducing a fixed integration step does not repair an inconsistent event representation. Distinguish electromechanical/RMS, dynamic-phasor and full electromagnetic-transient models by their retained states and time scales.

Read the complete relevant [ANDES — dynamic modelling and analysis manual](../sources/ANDES-Modeling-and-Analysis-Manual.lingua#r_5JM9DVGXWSD8645484SZP5XRSZ), [Hybrid Symbolic-Numeric Framework — Cui, Li and Tomsovic](../sources/Hybrid-Symbolic-Numeric-Power-Models-Cui.lingua#r_7XTYA62FQ8W2X448XXVFNPA7AK) and [DPsim — electromagnetic-transient and dynamic-phasor methods](../sources/DPsim-Transient-and-Dynamic-Phasor-Methods.lingua#r_6Y8PGZBGJHGV3JHZ1Q8XC77RR3) methods. Compare independent small analytical/discrete limits, step refinement, event-time sensitivity and energy/constraint closure. Inspect saturation, deadbands, relay logic and controller delays. Published agreement for a benchmark is evidence for its particular model family; every new device/limit combination needs the corresponding verification and a physical validation argument.

**Continue:** [Grid-following current control, synchronization and limits](../conversion/Grid-following-current-control-synchronization-and-limits.lingua#r_6RBJ2AJVKVGPF9HP5XP3EHYY5T).

